   "text": "I read the drawing as a 2-methoxy-tetrahydropyran carrying a hept-6-enoate ester, a pent-4-enyl chain and an N-PMB thiazolidin-2-one. I assigned the stereocentres by hand from the wedge and hash bonds, so the @/@@ labels are the least certain part.\n\n**Ring and substituents**\n- **Pyran ring:** six-membered, with the ring O at the bottom left. Going around from the O:\n  - C2 is the anomeric carbon. It carries OMe on a bold wedge and the thiazolidinone on a plain bond.\n  - C3 is CH2.\n  - C4 is CH and carries the ester O on a bold wedge.\n  - C5 is CH2.\n  - C6 is CH and carries the pentenyl chain on a hashed bond.\n- **Ester:** C(=O) followed by four CH2 groups and then CH=CH2, which is hept-6-enoate. The chain length is my best count of the vertices in the drawing.\n- **Alkyl chain on C6:** CH2CH2CH2CH=CH2, a pent-4-enyl group.\n- **Thiazolidinone:** the ring runs N(PMB)\u2013C4'(H)\u2013CH2\u2013S\u2013C(=O), closing back to N.\n  - C4' joins the pyran C2 and has its H on a bold wedge.\n  - PMB is the 4-methoxybenzyl group, CH2-C6H4-OMe.\n\n**Stereo assignments:** working through each centre from the 2D positions of its neighbours and the wedge or hash bond gave @@ at pyran C6, C4 and C2, and at thiazolidinone C4'.\n\nSMILES: C=CCCC[C@@H]1C[C@@H](OC(=O)CCCCC=C)C[C@@](OC)(O1)[C@@H]2CSC(=O)N2Cc1ccc(OC)cc1"
